From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: Media3D transforms, Clip, and what React Native sets on elements

OneDrive's interface is React Native for Windows, which makes its views from Windows.UI.Xaml elements and stopped at each missing piece. Added: Media3D PerspectiveTransform3D and CompositeTransform3D with UIElement.Transform3D (kept, an element is drawn flat); RectangleGeometry and UIElement.Clip, which is drawn (an element shows only inside its clip); the statics and accessors of UIElement's Projection, CacheMode, Transitions, IsTapEnabled, IsDoubleTapEnabled, IsRightTapEnabled, IsHoldingEnabled and ManipulationMode; Control's statics 2 to 7 (CornerRadiusProperty, BackgroundSizing, the attached IsTemplateFocusTarget and IsTemplateKeyTipTarget, focus engagement, XYFocus); TextBlock.TextTrimming, whose ellipsis cuts a line to the block's width (IsTextTrimmed tells), and TextHighlighters. UIElement.Shadow and Transform3D no longer release the caller's reference, and take null.
---
